<p>This did not test other browsers, a screen reader, copying a link address, dark-mode contrast, or saved favorites. Passing the checks is not a WCAG conformance result. WCAG's keyboard criterion concerns operating functionality through a keyboard interface; it is a reason to examine the missing behavior, rather than a certificate issued by this small test.<sup><a href="#rp-ref-keyboard">3</a></sup></p>

<section id="rp-destination" tabindex="-1">
  <h2>The fictional destination is here</h2>
  <p class="dek">Both cards point to this section. Only one needs a click handler to reach it.</p>
  <p>The useful review question is visible in the markup: where does this control go, and which separate control changes state? A resource title can answer the first question with <code>href</code>. The small marking control can answer the second on its own.</p>
</section>

